From d118952030496d43b71fbe1b78ac83fe5029e4f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:36:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: identify disk-record open and decode failures with
 raw offsets

Convert eight existing reader diagnostics, retaining non-dropping Error,
function/position wording, original I/O and false returns. The three
byte-identical decode calls share an event differentiated by SourceFunction.
Fixed signed file/unsigned offset metadata precedes copied bounded Error
so long exception detail cannot displace the location; existing truncation
flags remain the contract. No formatter, adapter, registry or reader changes.

Add a public reader case with owned absent/empty files and a valid disk
envelope containing one payload byte. Cover raw offset underflow, missing
file, envelope-read failure, successful tiny raw read followed by block
decode failure, plus transaction/undo-record open and decode errors. Check
actual messages, numeric positions, false returns and unchanged raw output
on early failures. No large allocation, private hook, real block acceptance,
production data or native-specific header/limit fields.

Shared eCash reader owner: these APIs/error paths predate ABC1fb7db17,
including99f7dd2d8b8/a51b28b23a2. Source lint/diff pass; native case remains
NOT_COMPILED/NOT_RUN. Sealed381/current final integration unchanged.

